  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 12.75,
      "end": 19.71,
      "text": "Yes, good evening. It's the Friday Rock Show. Sadly, this week minus Mr. Tommy Vance.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.71,
      "end": 25.71,
      "text": "Hi, this is Richard Skinner. Now, last week, I went down with the flu and Tommy sat in on the Rock On program for me.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.71,
      "end": 31.71,
      "text": "This week, Tommy's got flu, so I'm happy to return the compliment and we've got some great stuff too for you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.71,
      "end": 38.94,
      "text": "This week, live music from the band Trilogy. Also, two archive sessions of Lunacy from the Bonzo Dog Doodah Band,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.94,
      "end": 46.42,
      "text": "our band recorded back in 1968 and 1969 especially for radio one news plus we've got some electric",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.42,
      "end": 57.82,
      "text": "cuts on record too oh and tommy get well soon mate ufo from their new lp called making contact",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 555.44,
      "end": 560.38,
      "text": "a track called the way the wild wind blows now if you ever see that album you won't miss it in the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 560.38,
      "end": 564.9,
      "text": "record shop because it has a picture of a lady organist that i i never saw anybody like that",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 564.9,
      "end": 570.0,
      "text": "lady in church i tell you and before that over the edge from the status quo lp just supposing",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 570.48,
      "end": 572.12,
      "text": "And that was especially for Paul Wilbert.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 572.2,
      "end": 573.34,
      "text": "Paul, thanks for writing in to Tommy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 573.74,
      "end": 575.46,
      "text": "You live at number four, Crawley View.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 575.62,
      "end": 578.14,
      "text": "It says here, Poburn, Anwick or Elwick.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 578.24,
      "end": 579.84,
      "text": "I can't quite read that in Northumberland.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 579.9,
      "end": 581.22,
      "text": "Anyway, Paul, hi to you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 581.3,
      "end": 583.84,
      "text": "Also, hello to Vince, who lives in Stonehall.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 583.94,
      "end": 587.28,
      "text": "And also, all your mates that go to the Haxton Bridge High School.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 587.98,
      "end": 588.7,
      "text": "Stay listening.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 588.8,
      "end": 591.56,
      "text": "Some good music tonight, including some excellent stuff in session,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 591.56,
      "end": 596.16,
      "text": "produced by Tony Wilson, of the band Trilogy, a London-based trio.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 596.34,
      "end": 597.02,
      "text": "Surprise, surprise.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 597.02,
      "end": 600.02,
      "text": "Paul Dennis, Mark Bloxage and Nick Zimanek.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 600.78,
      "end": 602.22,
      "text": "Here's their first offering this evening.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 602.32,
      "end": 604.2,
      "text": "This is a track called A Legion in Morocco.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 605.48,
      "end": 610.28,
      "text": "It's the Friday Rock Show with Richard Skinner",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 610.28,
      "end": 895.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 900.0,
      "end": 1149.2,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1149.2,
      "end": 1151.64,
      "text": "sitting in for an ailing Tommy Vance.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1151.78,
      "end": 1153.72,
      "text": "And you just heard Trilogy, first of all,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1153.78,
      "end": 1155.16,
      "text": "with A Legion in Morocco,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1155.36,
      "end": 1156.94,
      "text": "first of their tracks in session this evening.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1157.32,
      "end": 1159.98,
      "text": "And then you heard Journey from their new LP Frontiers",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1159.98,
      "end": 1161.74,
      "text": "and Troubled Child.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1162.0,
      "end": 1163.84,
      "text": "Talk about so near and yet so far.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1164.26,
      "end": 1166.12,
      "text": "I was recently in California",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1166.12,
      "end": 1168.88,
      "text": "and got so close to getting an interview with Journey",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1168.88,
      "end": 1171.12,
      "text": "it was within an hour or two of the recording",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1171.12,
      "end": 1172.04,
      "text": "and they cancelled it",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1172.04,
      "end": 1174.42,
      "text": "but I'm told that at least one member of Journey",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1174.42,
      "end": 1176.4,
      "text": "will be coming over to England in the near future",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1176.4,
      "end": 1178.58,
      "text": "probably Scotland Wells and Northern Ireland as well",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1178.58,
      "end": 1179.24,
      "text": "come to think of it",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1179.24,
      "end": 1182.16,
      "text": "and hopefully we'll get a chat with him when he arrives",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1182.16,
      "end": 1183.82,
      "text": "whoever he is, that'll be in the future",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1183.82,
      "end": 1187.58,
      "text": "tonight, fascinating old stuff",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1187.58,
      "end": 1189.28,
      "text": "from the Bonzo Dog Doodah band",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1189.28,
      "end": 1192.86,
      "text": "recorded in session back in 1968 and 1969",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1192.86,
      "end": 1194.26,
      "text": "for Radio 1",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1194.26,
      "end": 1198.9,
      "text": "This first session, from March 1968, that's nearly 15 years old,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1199.24,
      "end": 1202.48,
      "text": "features the legendary Doodah Band line-up, and let's run through it.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1202.54,
      "end": 1204.0,
      "text": "Viv Stanshaw on vocals and trumpet,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1204.42,
      "end": 1207.9,
      "text": "Neil Innes on vocals and piano, now he produced most of the band's stuff as well,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1208.32,
      "end": 1212.58,
      "text": "Roger Ruskin-Spear, who supervised things like The Dummies and The Robots,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1212.84,
      "end": 1214.12,
      "text": "Rodney Slater on saxophone,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1214.34,
      "end": 1215.84,
      "text": "Legs Larry Smith on drums,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1216.46,
      "end": 1219.58,
      "text": "Vernon Dudley-Bohay-Knowell on guitar and banjo,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1219.92,
      "end": 1222.74,
      "text": "and Sam Spoons, that's Martin Stafford, on percussion.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1223.12,
      "end": 1224.44,
      "text": "It does sound like the intro and the outro.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1224.58,
      "end": 1225.56,
      "text": "That isn't in this session.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1225.64,
      "end": 1228.14,
      "text": "What we do have coming up for you now is three marvellous tracks.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1228.44,
      "end": 1231.46,
      "text": "Eight minutes of music, Do the Trouser Press, Canyons of Your Mind,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1231.98,
      "end": 1234.18,
      "text": "and the top five hit of I'm the Urban Spaceman.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1234.38,
      "end": 1235.98,
      "text": "First, let's do the Trouser Press.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1236.68,
      "end": 1354.27,
      "text": "Program you've just been listening to is a recording of a new play by G.G. Dunhill",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1354.27,
      "end": 1357.31,
      "text": "in one act for eight albatrosses in the reservoir.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1357.89,
      "end": 1360.27,
      "text": "The part of Gooch was played by a frying pan.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1360.67,
      "end": 1363.17,
      "text": "The other parts of Gooch were played by...",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1363.17,
      "end": 1370.97,
      "text": "Urban Spaceman, that's Bonzo Dog Doodah Band, recorded on 29th of March, 1968.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1725.1,
      "end": 1728.58,
      "text": "Before that, you heard The Canyons of Your Mind, and do the trouser press.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1728.58,
      "end": 1733.66,
      "text": "This is a tribute to Geno Washington, the band with the sweet essence of giraffe.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1733.66,
      "end": 1734.66,
      "text": "Oh, what a line.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1734.9,
      "end": 1737.08,
      "text": "I just wonder what programme that was recorded for originally.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1737.22,
      "end": 1738.98,
      "text": "Probably the Jimmy Young Show or something like that.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1739.62,
      "end": 1742.84,
      "text": "A bit of Eric Clapton coming up now from his LP Money and Cigarettes",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1742.84,
      "end": 1746.84,
      "text": "out on the wonderful Duck Records label, produced by Tom Dowd.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1746.92,
      "end": 1749.76,
      "text": "The album also featuring the guitars of Rykuda and Albert Lee as well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1750.02,
      "end": 1751.62,
      "text": "This is a song called Ain't Going Down.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1752.26,
      "end": 1760.06,
      "text": "Sort of tenuous link in that little segue two in a row there.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1980.0,
      "end": 2179.42,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2179.42,
      "end": 2183.04,
      "text": "That was the Yardbirds from their legendary LP Roger the Engineer,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2183.26,
      "end": 2187.06,
      "text": "originally done in 1966, and out again on the Edsel label.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2187.06,
      "end": 2189.42,
      "text": "that's Rack My Mind you heard there",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2189.42,
      "end": 2191.32,
      "text": "and before that Eric Clapton from the",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2191.32,
      "end": 2192.94,
      "text": "more recent and brand new album",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2192.94,
      "end": 2195.24,
      "text": "Money and Cigarettes and Ain't Going Down",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2195.24,
      "end": 2197.28,
      "text": "the Yardbirds line up on that recording of",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2197.28,
      "end": 2199.6,
      "text": "Rack My Mind was Chris J. Drazier",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2199.6,
      "end": 2201.12,
      "text": "I can never say his name right",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2201.12,
      "end": 2202.84,
      "text": "Jim McCarty, Jeff Beck",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2202.84,
      "end": 2204.88,
      "text": "Keith Ralph and Ian Samuel Smith",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2204.88,
      "end": 2207.52,
      "text": "recorded at the Advision Studios just around the corner",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2207.52,
      "end": 2209.28,
      "text": "I was walking past there today and somebody",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2209.28,
      "end": 2210.56,
      "text": "says what happens here?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2211.04,
      "end": 2213.42,
      "text": "That was a chap called Andrew Turner who reads the news on Radio 1",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2213.42,
      "end": 2215.3,
      "text": "and I said a few people have recorded some",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2215.3,
      "end": 2219.58,
      "text": "excellent records in there and that was just one of them friday rock show richard skinner for tommy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2219.58,
      "end": 2224.94,
      "text": "vance and we now join the canadian broadcasting system this is a track from triumph's lp never",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2224.94,
      "end": 2230.84,
      "text": "surrender but first the headlines the labor department reports that during the week was",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2230.84,
      "end": 2235.44,
      "text": "whittled away in the final hour of grading to a close and let me tell you that is what i said",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2235.44,
      "end": 2246.24,
      "text": "before a falsehood let me tell you that is what i said before a speculation triumph their album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2551.98,
      "end": 2554.26,
      "text": "never surrender and that was too much thinking",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2554.26,
      "end": 2555.98,
      "text": "too much American radio",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2555.98,
      "end": 2557.92,
      "text": "never listen to too much American radio",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2557.92,
      "end": 2559.28,
      "text": "it drives you round the twist, it really does",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2559.28,
      "end": 2561.9,
      "text": "on British Radio 1, the Friday night",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2561.9,
      "end": 2564.2,
      "text": "connection takes place in just a few minutes time",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2564.2,
      "end": 2565.5,
      "text": "before that we've got",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2565.5,
      "end": 2567.52,
      "text": "oh I'll tell you what, I'll also tell you that the winner",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2567.52,
      "end": 2570.28,
      "text": "of last week's connection comes from Southampton",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2570.28,
      "end": 2572.12,
      "text": "in Hampshire, one of my old stomping grounds",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2572.12,
      "end": 2574.04,
      "text": "I'll say no more, so if you're listening in the",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2574.04,
      "end": 2575.86,
      "text": "Southampton area, it could be you",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2575.86,
      "end": 2577.8,
      "text": "that's coming up in about ten minutes time",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2577.8,
      "end": 2579.76,
      "text": "before that, a bit of music from",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2579.76,
      "end": 2581.82,
      "text": "Canada, a band called Headpins",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2581.82,
      "end": 2584.72,
      "text": "and before that, a second one tonight from Trilogy,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2584.84,
      "end": 2586.44,
      "text": "a song called Necrosleep.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2587.02,
      "end": 2587.72,
      "text": "And don't you dare.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2588.0,
      "end": 2590.56,
      "text": "It sort of fades in quietly, as Mr Peel would say.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2590.76,
      "end": 2591.58,
      "text": "It's a quarter to eleven.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2592.2,
      "end": 2595.2,
      "text": "Pretty good, isn't it?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2595.2,
      "end": 3055.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3060.0,
      "end": 3192.1,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3192.1,
      "end": 3193.2,
      "text": "That's called Turn It Loud.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3193.64,
      "end": 3196.68,
      "text": "Headpins on the Atco label and an LP called Turn It Loud.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3197.12,
      "end": 3198.3,
      "text": "And before that, you heard Trilogy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3198.3,
      "end": 3202.22,
      "text": "and their second track this evening in session, Necrosleep.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3202.46,
      "end": 3203.48,
      "text": "It's five to eleven.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3211.09,
      "end": 3213.53,
      "text": "The music for the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3213.97,
      "end": 3216.75,
      "text": "And having said that, the winner of last week's Connection",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3216.75,
      "end": 3218.33,
      "text": "comes from the Southampton area.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3218.83,
      "end": 3220.83,
      "text": "I then read an extremely long and detailed",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3220.83,
      "end": 3223.57,
      "text": "and correct letter for last week's competition",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3223.57,
      "end": 3225.41,
      "text": "and discovered there is no name on it.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3225.47,
      "end": 3226.81,
      "text": "So all I can say is congratulations",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3226.81,
      "end": 3229.79,
      "text": "to the occupier of the house called Malens",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3229.79,
      "end": 3231.29,
      "text": "at number nine, Limeclose,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3231.71,
      "end": 3233.51,
      "text": "Dibden-Purley, Southampton, in Hants,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3233.91,
      "end": 3235.35,
      "text": "SO9 5RD.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3235.51,
      "end": 3237.07,
      "text": "Congratulations to the occupant",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3237.07,
      "end": 3239.63,
      "text": "who rightly recognised that the three tracks",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3239.63,
      "end": 3241.85,
      "text": "played in the Friday Night Connection last week",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3241.85,
      "end": 3242.79,
      "text": "were as follows.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3243.23,
      "end": 3246.01,
      "text": "Peter Gabriel from the album Peter Gabriel, of course,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3246.01,
      "end": 3251.53,
      "text": "with wallflower followed by how you're going to see me now alice cooper from the lp from the",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3251.53,
      "end": 3256.97,
      "text": "inside then you heard white rabbit jefferson airplane from their album flight log we play that",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3256.97,
      "end": 3263.31,
      "text": "their greatest hits from 1966 to 1976 the connection then between peter gabriel's wallflower",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3263.31,
      "end": 3268.22,
      "text": "how are you going to see me now by alice cooper and jefferson airplanes white rabbit quite rightly",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3268.22,
      "end": 3272.5,
      "text": "it's been pointed out that the connection has to be alice in wonderland because the white rabbit",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3272.5,
      "end": 3273.34,
      "text": "It appears at the beginning.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3274.0,
      "end": 3275.98,
      "text": "Alice appears most of the time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3276.66,
      "end": 3278.72,
      "text": "And most ingenious, perhaps, the Mad Hatter",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3278.72,
      "end": 3281.08,
      "text": "is the logo of the Charisma record label",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3281.08,
      "end": 3282.62,
      "text": "on which Peter Gabriel records.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3282.74,
      "end": 3285.24,
      "text": "So that is the connection on last week's Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3285.84,
      "end": 3288.78,
      "text": "This week, the mysterious person down in Hampshire",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3288.78,
      "end": 3291.0,
      "text": "has got together an intriguing connection,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3291.44,
      "end": 3292.96,
      "text": "one that I hope that you'll get together",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3292.96,
      "end": 3296.02,
      "text": "over the next, ooh, 18 minutes or so.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3296.08,
      "end": 3296.78,
      "text": "Here's part one.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3296.78,
      "end": 3308.75,
      "text": "Has the dawn ever seen your eyes?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3308.75,
      "end": 3311.75,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3311.75,
      "end": 4438.66,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4438.66,
      "end": 4443.48,
      "text": "Now, if you know the connection between those three tracks set by our anonymous listener",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4443.48,
      "end": 4446.42,
      "text": "who listened all the way from Dibden-Furley near Southampton,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4446.88,
      "end": 4449.68,
      "text": "then send in your connection for The Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4449.68,
      "end": 4455.08,
      "text": "To Tommy Vance, the Friday Rock Show, Radio 1, London, W1A, 4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4455.78,
      "end": 4457.72,
      "text": "Don't forget also to set your own connection,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4458.54,
      "end": 4461.7,
      "text": "and then you'll win a prize and hopefully baffle a whole lot of other people.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4461.94,
      "end": 4465.48,
      "text": "It's the Friday Night Connection, Tommy Vance, the Friday Night Rock Show,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4466.12,
      "end": 4469.68,
      "text": "BBC, Radio 1, London, W1A, 4WW.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4470.64,
      "end": 4473.08,
      "text": "And good luck. Stand by for some Hendrix Oldie.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4473.62,
      "end": 4517.22,
      "text": "Or me. Love you just the same.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4517.22,
      "end": 4539.85,
      "text": "1968.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4542.04,
      "end": 4545.04,
      "text": "...Hendrix and Voodoo Child.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4545.04,
      "end": 4675.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4680.0,
      "end": 4840.14,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4840.14,
      "end": 4843.24,
      "text": "That was number one in October 1970, soon after his death.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4843.3,
      "end": 4846.62,
      "text": "Now available again on the Jimi Hendrix singles album,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4846.74,
      "end": 4848.48,
      "text": "which has been put out again by Polydor.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4848.82,
      "end": 4850.5,
      "text": "And a goodbye if your records are wearing out.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4851.02,
      "end": 4853.2,
      "text": "Another track now from our session from Trilogy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4853.28,
      "end": 4854.12,
      "text": "This is Arctic Life.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4854.78,
      "end": 4857.78,
      "text": "Benatar, a superstar in America.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5220.0,
      "end": 5386.49,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5386.49,
      "end": 5388.23,
      "text": "Perhaps she ought to be more successful over here.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5388.33,
      "end": 5389.23,
      "text": "Shadows of the Night.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5389.23,
      "end": 5391.77,
      "text": "A near-hit single for her",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5391.77,
      "end": 5395.29,
      "text": "And before that, a trilogy from their session for this programme this evening",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5395.29,
      "end": 5396.47,
      "text": "An Arctic Life",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5396.47,
      "end": 5400.29,
      "text": "Talking of sessions, it's back to July 1969 now",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5400.29,
      "end": 5402.73,
      "text": "As we catch up with the Bonzo Dog, Doodah Band",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5402.73,
      "end": 5406.29,
      "text": "And a few more wonderful bits of idiocy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5406.29,
      "end": 6016.54,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5482.53,
      "end": 5484.63,
      "text": "Everybody knows he's the greatest man.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5495.93,
      "end": 5497.13,
      "text": "Makes a hell of a...",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5497.13,
      "end": 5546.4,
      "text": "Kick the sand right back in their faces.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5546.84,
      "end": 5547.18,
      "text": "Kick!",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5556.42,
      "end": 5599.02,
      "text": "You arseholes speak loud for big muscles.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5629.2,
      "end": 5630.08,
      "text": "One person bending.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6016.54,
      "end": 6019.02,
      "text": "Eat your heart out, Bobby, Boris, Pickett and the Crip Kickers.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6019.08,
      "end": 6022.18,
      "text": "That was the Bonzo Dog Band's version of Monster Mash.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6022.36,
      "end": 6023.22,
      "text": "Before that, Tent.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6023.7,
      "end": 6026.42,
      "text": "And before that, the strongest man in the world, Mr Apollo,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6026.64,
      "end": 6029.56,
      "text": "recorded in July 1969 for Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6030.16,
      "end": 6031.7,
      "text": "Not long after that, about a year later,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6031.7,
      "end": 6033.98,
      "text": "The band broke up, unfortunately.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6034.4,
      "end": 6037.8,
      "text": "Fifth Stanchel went on to become a bit of a personality all over, I suppose.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6038.26,
      "end": 6042.24,
      "text": "Neil Innes, of course, a prolific composer, working with Grimm's and many other people.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6042.8,
      "end": 6044.76,
      "text": "Roger Ruskin-Spear, I don't know what he's doing now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6044.84,
      "end": 6048.48,
      "text": "Other people left the business, and some of them turned into Bodker's Whoopie Band.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6049.1,
      "end": 6051.12,
      "text": "All in all, though, an excellent group in their day.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6051.62,
      "end": 6054.1,
      "text": "And thanks to the Bonzo Dogs, what a lovely old session that was.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6054.76,
      "end": 6057.02,
      "text": "A bit more of our session for Trilogy coming up later,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6057.02,
      "end": 6061.54,
      "text": "but first it's time for the staff choice, the staff selection on the programme tonight.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6061.7,
      "end": 6065.28,
      "text": "One chosen by Tony Wilson, one by Tommy Vance just before he went sick.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6065.64,
      "end": 6068.48,
      "text": "First of all, Tommy's selection, The Pink Fairies from 1971.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6069.18,
      "end": 6069.88,
      "text": "Say you love me.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6070.54,
      "end": 6077.74,
      "text": "Tony Wilson's staff selection for this week, Jessica from the Ormond Brothers.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6077.74,
      "end": 6295.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6300.0,
      "end": 6725.89,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6725.89,
      "end": 6727.97,
      "text": "Here's the last one from Paul, Mark and Nick.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6728.19,
      "end": 6729.61,
      "text": "Trilogy. This is Dark Hunter.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6730.57,
      "end": 6733.57,
      "text": "Dark Hunter. Trilogy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7044.7,
      "end": 7046.88,
      "text": "And that's it for this Friday Rock Show this week.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7046.96,
      "end": 7049.74,
      "text": "My thanks to my producer, Tony Wilson, who put the music together.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7050.02,
      "end": 7051.5,
      "text": "All the best, too, to Tommy Vance.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7051.5,
      "end": 7054.6,
      "text": "Tommy, I hope you'll be back for the Top 40 show on Sunday.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7054.6,
      "end": 7055.6,
      "text": "All the best to you, Tommy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7056.3,
      "end": 7059.46,
      "text": "One thing's for sure, I'll be here with Rock On tomorrow at 5 o'clock.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7059.74,
      "end": 7062.26,
      "text": "But now, Radio 1's transmitters are closing down.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7062.98,
      "end": 7065.84,
      "text": "We'll be back on the air tomorrow morning at 6 with Adrian John.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7065.96,
      "end": 7066.8,
      "text": "Wake up to the weekend.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7067.38,
      "end": 7071.98,
      "text": "In the meantime, my message to you, snuggle down, keep warm and sleep tight.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7072.34,
      "end": 7073.56,
      "text": "Good night. Look after yourself.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    }
  ]
}